rewamp: EGL_ANGLE_context_virtualization for the WGL (desktop OpenGL) backend.

DisplayWGL backs EVERY EGL context with the display's single native WGL
context ("contexts are virtualized"). A WGL context can only be current on one
thread at a time, so a second, shared EGL context made current on another
thread fails with EGL_CONTEXT_LOST (DisplayWGL::makeCurrent). projectM's preset
preloader needs exactly that (compile the next preset on a worker thread).

This brings DisplayEGL's model to DisplayWGL: a context created with
EGL_CONTEXT_VIRTUALIZATION_GROUP_ANGLE gets its own RendererWGL / native
context, created by wglCreateContextAttribsARB in the main context's share
list. The calling thread's native context is restored after the renderer is
built. Sharing across renderers relies on glProgramUniform* (GL 4.1+), which
ProgramExecutableGL uses when present; textures/buffers use the calling
context's state manager.

